  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "The United States holds midterm elections for 435 House members and five non-voting delegates, 35 Senate seats including special elections in Florida and Ohio, and 39 state and territorial governors.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-03:10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "Elections were held on November 3, 2026, during the second term of Republican president Donald Trump.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383861407:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "The war with Iran became a subject of Democratic campaigning ahead of the November 3 midterms.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1383861407:147"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "Of the 35 Senate races, Democrats won 20 and Republicans won 13, with 2 not yet called.",
      "cites": [
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:the-senate-table"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:00:31Z",
      "text": "Democrats gained seats in Iowa, North Carolina, Kansas, Maine, Ohio, South Carolina and Texas.",
      "cites": [
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-ia",
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-nc",
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-ks",
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-me",
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-oh-special",
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-sc",
        "elex:2026-united-states-senate-elections:senate-tx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:00:39Z",
      "text": "Of the 36 governor's races, Democrats won 22 and Republicans won 12, with 2 not yet called.",
      "cites": [
        "elex:2026-united-states-gubernatorial-elections:governors-table"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:00:45Z",
      "text": "Democrats gained governorships in Georgia, Iowa, Nevada, Ohio and Texas.",
      "cites": [
        "elex:2026-united-states-gubernatorial-elections:governors-ga",
        "elex:2026-united-states-gubernatorial-elections:governors-ia",
        "elex:2026-united-states-gubernatorial-elections:governors-nv",
        "elex:2026-united-states-gubernatorial-elections:governors-oh",
        "elex:2026-united-states-gubernatorial-elections:governors-tx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:00:53Z",
      "text": "In the House, Democrats hold 251 seats and Republicans 153, with 31 still to be called; a majority is 218 seats.",
      "cites": [
        "elex:2026-united-states-house-of-representatives-elections:house-infobox"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:00:59Z",
      "text": "On the race tables, 41 districts changed party, and 49 are not yet called.",
      "cites": [
        "elex:2026-united-states-house-of-representatives-elections:house-table"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:01:07Z",
      "text": "Readers also turned to the article on United States midterm elections, which drew 244,478 readers.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:United_States_midterm_election:2026-11-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:01:11Z",
      "text": "The James Talarico article drew 105,766 readers, and the 2026 United States Senate elections article drew 90,787.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:James_Talarico:2026-11-03",
        "views:en:2026_United_States_Senate_elections:2026-11-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:01:16Z",
      "text": "On 3 November 2026, 455,194 people read the article on 2026 United States elections, about 18 times the usual daily readership.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:2026_United_States_elections:2026-11-03",
        "views:en:2026_United_States_elections:prior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:01:23Z",
      "text": "The article was read in 10 languages, and after English, the most readers were in Persian, with 28,399.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:2026_United_States_elections:2026-11-03",
        "views:fa:انتخابات_۲۰۲۶_ایالات_متحده_آمریکا:2026-11-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:01:30Z",
      "text": "On the globe, each language glows where it is mainly spoken, brighter for more readers; a language is not a country.",
      "cites": [
        "views:fa:انتخابات_۲۰۲۶_ایالات_متحده_آمریکا:2026-11-03",
        "views:pt:Eleições_nos_Estados_Unidos_em_2026:2026-11-03",
        "views:de:Wahlen_in_den_Vereinigten_Staaten_2026:2026-11-03",
        "views:fr:Élections_de_2026_aux_États-Unis:2026-11-03",
        "views:zh:2026年美國選舉:2026-11-03",
        "views:it:Elezioni_parlamentari_negli_Stati_Uniti_d'America_del_2026:2026-11-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:01:40Z",
      "text": "The Guardian and Reuters reported on this story.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-03:10",
        "wiki:2026-11-03:11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-03T00:01:48Z",
      "text": "Sources include Wikipedia, Current events, Wikipedia articles, Wikimedia pageviews and Wikidata, and each caption links to its evidence.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-03:10",
        "wiki:rev:1383861407:147",
